STAGE-1 EXPEDIENT: cut autoconf's html documentation build.

THIS PRODUCES A PACKAGE THAT MUST BE REBUILT. It belongs in
hpkg-out/arm64/stage1/ and must never be published to a shipping repository.

makeinfo cannot run in this image at all: the texinfo_bootstrap package ships the
Texinfo/ directory but *zero* .pm files, so texi2any dies in its BEGIN block with
"Can't locate Texinfo/ModulePath.pm in @INC" under any perl. Building a real
texinfo first is not possible yet -- its dependencies form a 10-deep cycle:
texinfo -> libintl -> groff -> pnmcrop/netpbm -> libjasper -> cmake -> libcurl
-> libpsl -> libidn2 -> gtkdocize.

Emptying HTMLS is preferred over stubbing makeinfo: install-html-am then has no
prerequisites, so the doc/*.html rules never run and no bogus placeholder files
are installed. The prebuilt .info files in the tarball are still installed by
"make install", so info documentation is not lost.

Two other cuts do NOT work here, both worth knowing:
  - MAKEINFO=true: the rule is followed by "mv doc/autoconf.htp doc/autoconf.html",
    so the command must actually create its -o file.
  - touching the doc targets (the idiom this recipe already uses for man/*.1 and
    configure): defeated by the guest's clock skew.

Note also that the doc rule uses $(MAKEINFOHTML) (Makefile:323, expanded by the
doc/autoconf.html rule at Makefile:1055), not $(MAKEINFO), and that `all` never
depends on $(HTMLS) -- only install-html does. That is why patching BUILD()
cannot fix this and INSTALL() is the right place.

Applies to: input-source-packages/develop/sources/autoconf-2.72-1/autoconf-2.72.recipe
--- a/autoconf-2.72.recipe
+++ b/autoconf-2.72.recipe
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@
 INSTALL()
 {
 	make install
-	make install-html
+	make install-html HTMLS=
 }
 
 TEST()
